From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:06:07 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: spoof Neo screen work area with native accessors

Complete Screen.availLeft/availTop/availWidth/availHeight using native,
read-only prototype accessors. Use a 24 CSS-pixel menu bar and an
auto-hidden Dock on a single primary display. Bound the top inset to
emulated screen height and saturate available height for tiny screens.

Pin a chosen base MacBook Neo display profile: 1204x753 CSS pixels at 2x
(2408x1506 physical panel pixels), with a 1100x650 content viewport. These
are explicit spoofed assumptions, not measured Apple default settings.
Honor existing CDP metrics overrides and reset behavior.

Keep device-width/device-height media features tied to effective screen
metrics rather than the content viewport. Invalidate stylesheet caches
before media-query callbacks on metrics changes. Replace the root-element
1920px fallback with its owning frame's effective viewport width.

Update existing default-dependent test expectations and give fixed-size
screenshot/media-query tests explicit metrics; add no unit tests. Do not
change Window outer geometry, UA/client hints, worker loading, or GPU APIs.

References:
https://www.apple.com/macbook-neo/specs/
https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/refs/heads/main/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/screen.idl
https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-view/#the-screen-interface
https://drafts.csswg.org/mediaqueries-4/#device-width
